<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederik X</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1968</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Frederik X of Denmark</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederik X is King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, who succeeded on 14 January 2024 when his mother, Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margrethe-ii">Margrethe II</a>, abdicated. Before his accession he served for decades as crown prince, trained in the armed forces and studied political science. He is married to Queen Mary, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, and their eldest son, Christian, is crown prince.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederik-x.jpg" alt="Frederik X" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Finnish Government · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Frederik_X_in_2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
